WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.646 --> 00:00:03.229
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.200
- Baking is my communication
tool with American people.

00:00:11.162 --> 00:00:13.950
I'm not so good speak English,

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.660
but I can make a good dessert.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.860
So during the holiday, I'm always making

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.673
a Japanese Christmas shortcake.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.440
- I'm Nico Tortorella.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.020
I'm an actor, an activist

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.190
and a firm believer that our differences

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.120
actually make us stronger.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.700
I'm on a journey with
IKEA to meet real people

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.900
and discover the diverse
and spectacular ways

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.565
they celebrate the holidays.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.161
Maybe you celebrate Christmas
with milk and cookies

00:00:44.161 --> 00:00:45.430
and a Christmas ham.

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:48.300
Or maybe you celebrate it
with fried chicken and cake

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.425
like Portland resident Mio Asaka.

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:52.470
- My name is Mio Asaka.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:56.583
I'm a baker and owner
of Mio's Delectables.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.350
- Mio runs a mini Japanese bakery

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:00.330
right out of her own home

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.180
and sells her goods at the
Portland Farmers’ Market.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.460
Mio has this real passion for baking

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.290
and sharing the traditions
that she brought from Japan.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:11.432
Her specialty: the
Japanese Christmas cake.

00:01:11.432 --> 00:01:12.978
(angelic choir)

00:01:12.978 --> 00:01:14.469
Mmm.

00:01:14.469 --> 00:01:16.722
(playful music)

00:01:16.722 --> 00:01:17.680
We should probably go
get some strawberries

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.712
for this cake, huh?

00:01:18.712 --> 00:01:19.890
- [Mio] Yeah, yeah.

00:01:20.098 --> 00:01:21.426
- Wow, hi.

00:01:21.426 --> 00:01:22.428
How are you?

00:01:22.828 --> 00:01:25.410
Mio's Delectables isn't
just a business for Mio.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.720
It's a way for her to share her traditions

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.480
and culture with other people

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.674
and to really bring people together,

00:01:31.674 --> 00:01:33.233
especially during the holidays.

00:01:35.671 --> 00:01:37.202
(knocking on door)

00:01:37.552 --> 00:01:38.933
Hi!

00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:40.102
How are you?

00:01:40.102 --> 00:01:40.935
Good to see you.

00:01:40.935 --> 00:01:41.768
- Good to see you.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:42.663
Welcome.

00:01:42.663 --> 00:01:43.496
Come in.

00:01:43.496 --> 00:01:44.780
- I come bearing gifts.
- Oh, wow.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:48.130
My Christmas tree is like this size tree,

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:52.610
but I always decoration.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.310
You have to enjoy that.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:55.455
- This is your son here?

00:01:55.455 --> 00:01:57.377
- [Mio] Yes.
- [Nico] Willie?

00:01:57.377 --> 00:01:59.470
- William.
- William.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.530
I admire Mio for being a single mother

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.060
who works hard to create a warm, inviting

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.850
and loving home for her family.

00:02:06.668 --> 00:02:08.109
Ta-da!

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.730
Japanese Christmas is pretty unique.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.880
For a while, it was a really
romantic holiday in Japan,

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.090
kind of like Valentine's
Day in the United States.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.700
- [All] Romance.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.625
- Fried chicken is really popular.

00:02:23.625 --> 00:02:25.020
- [All] Karaage.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.690
- And dessert—Christmas cake, especially—

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.113
is a focal point for Japanese Christmas.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:37.260
- [Mio] When I came to the
U.S., I didn't know that

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:40.920
this country not familiar
with Japanese style

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.920
type of cake, so I explained this cake is

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.840
a very soft and not too sweet.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.781
Now it is very popular.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.160
- This looks so beautiful.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.010
Japanese Christmas cake originated in

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:55.510
post-World War II Japan.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:58.070
Middle-class citizens
finally had access to sugar

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.900
and other ingredients that had once been

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.270
considered exclusive.

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:03.773
And from this, the tradition was born.

00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:04.925
All right, it's time to eat.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:12.010
- [Mio] Japanese Christmas
is an important day.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:15.660
We eat a big dinner with our family.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:20.660
It's very much like the U.S.,
but we eat sushi and karaage.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:26.300
- [Nico] Do you have any
traditions before a Christmas meal?

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.312
- We say (speaking Japanese.)

00:03:29.312 --> 00:03:30.784
Bon appetit.
- Bon appetit.

00:03:30.784 --> 00:03:31.732
- (speaking Japanese)

00:03:31.732 --> 00:03:33.476
- (speaking Japanese)

00:03:33.476 --> 00:03:36.059
(gentle music)

00:03:36.927 --> 00:03:39.200
- Mio is pretty inspiring.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.950
She truly embodies the
tradition represented by

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.023
something as simple as a cake.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:48.360
Japanese Christmas cake
is a symbol for prosperity

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.910
and growth, qualities that Mio really

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.700
brings to life every
time she bakes this cake

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.354
for her friends and family.

00:04:02.388 --> 00:04:06.530
- (singing in Japanese)

00:04:07.544 --> 00:04:08.694
- There you have it, folks.

00:04:08.694 --> 00:04:10.113
Rudolph the red-nosed reindeer.

